## Stack & Versions

| Layer | Choice | Rationale |
|-------|--------|-----------|
| Framework | Next.js 15 (App Router) | Server Components by default, streaming, nested layouts |
| Runtime | Node.js 20+ | `crypto` global, native `fetch`, stable `node:` imports |
| Database | `better-sqlite3` | Synchronous, fast, zero network overhead for single-node deploys. Use Turso only if you need multi-region edge |
| ORM/Query | Drizzle ORM | Type-safe SQL, migrations in TypeScript, no codegen step |
| Auth | Lucia (or custom session) | Lightweight, works with SQLite, no OAuth lock-in |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS 3.4 | Utility-first, no runtime CSS-in-JS overhead |
| Forms | Server Actions + `react-hook-form` | Progressive enhancement, type-safe from server to client |
| Validation | Zod | Same schemas on server and client |
| Testing | Vitest + Playwright | Unit tests for utilities, E2E for critical flows |

**Non-negotiable:** We do not use `pg`, `mysql2`, or Prisma. SQLite is the source of truth. If you outgrow it, fork the project—don't bolt on complexity now.

